{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Laplace Approximation: Post-hoc Uncertainty for an Existing PyTorch Model\n","\n","This notebook starts with a trained deterministic PyTorch regression model and adds uncertainty **without retraining the entire network as a full BNN**.\n","\n","```text\n","trained PyTorch model\n","      ↓\n","MAP / deterministic weights\n","      ↓\n","last-layer Laplace approximation\n","      ↓\n","posterior predictive distribution\n","      ↓\n","capacity scenarios\n","      ↓\n","Pyomo + HiGHS\n","      ↓\n","risk-aware capacity planning\n","```\n","\n","Laplace approximation is a local Gaussian approximation around the MAP solution; it is not the exact full neural posterior.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import random, numpy as np, pandas as pd, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import torch, torch.nn as nn\n","from torch.utils.data import TensorDataset, DataLoader\n","from laplace import Laplace\n","import pyomo.environ as pyo\n","SEED=42\n","random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED); torch.set_default_dtype(torch.float32)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Synthetic production-capacity data\n","\n","Features: load, temperature, maintenance score, and shift experience. In a real system these could come from MES, SCADA, or IoT data.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["n=420\n","load=np.random.uniform(.35,.98,n); temp=np.random.normal(25,5,n); maintenance=np.random.uniform(.2,1,n); experience=np.random.uniform(.1,1,n)\n","true_mean=82+34*np.tanh(2.1*(load-.58))-.55*np.abs(temp-23)+12*maintenance+8*experience-15*(load-.84)**2\n","capacity=true_mean+np.random.normal(0,5.5,n)\n","Xr=np.column_stack([load,temp,maintenance,experience]).astype(np.float32); yr=capacity.astype(np.float32)\n","ntr=320; Xtrr,Xter=Xr[:ntr],Xr[ntr:]; ytrr,yte=yr[:ntr],yr[ntr:]\n","Xm,Xs=Xtrr.mean(0,keepdims=True),Xtrr.std(0,keepdims=True)+1e-6; ym,ys=float(ytrr.mean()),float(ytrr.std()+1e-6)\n","Xtr=torch.tensor((Xtrr-Xm)/Xs); Xte=torch.tensor((Xter-Xm)/Xs); ytr=torch.tensor(((ytrr-ym)/ys).reshape(-1,1)); ytest=torch.tensor(((yte-ym)/ys).reshape(-1,1))\n","train_loader=DataLoader(TensorDataset(Xtr,ytr),batch_size=64,shuffle=True)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Train the deterministic PyTorch model\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["class CapacityNet(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self,d=4):\n","        super().__init__(); self.feature_extractor=nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d,32),nn.Tanh(),nn.Linear(32,16),nn.Tanh()); self.output_layer=nn.Linear(16,1)\n","    def forward(self,x): return self.output_layer(self.feature_extractor(x))\n","model=CapacityNet(); opt=torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(),lr=.01,weight_decay=1e-4); mse=nn.MSELoss(); losses=[]\n","for epoch in range(900):\n","    total=0\n","    for xb,yb in train_loader:\n","        opt.zero_grad(); loss=mse(model(xb),yb); loss.backward(); opt.step(); total+=float(loss)*len(xb)\n","    losses.append(total/len(Xtr))\n","model.eval(); pred=(model(Xte).detach().squeeze(-1).numpy()*ys+ym); print('Deterministic test RMSE:',round(float(np.sqrt(np.mean((pred-yte)**2))),3))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Last-layer Laplace approximation\n","\n","The local approximation is\n","\n","\\[p(\\theta|D)\\approx N(\\theta_{MAP},H^{-1}).\n","\n","We use the last layer because it is a pragmatic, low-cost post-hoc uncertainty layer for an existing network.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["with torch.no_grad():\n","    residual=model(Xtr)-ytr; sigma_noise=float(torch.sqrt(torch.mean(residual**2)).clamp_min(1e-3))\n","la=Laplace(model,likelihood='regression',subset_of_weights='last_layer',hessian_structure='full',sigma_noise=sigma_noise,prior_precision=1.0,last_layer_name='output_layer')\n","la.fit(train_loader)\n","la.optimize_prior_precision(pred_type='glm',method='marglik',n_steps=80,lr=.08,prior_structure='scalar')\n","print('Noise SD in normalized units:',sigma_noise); print('Prior precision:',la.prior_precision)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Predictive uncertainty on the test set\n","\n","Function uncertainty and observation noise are combined approximately as\n","\n","\\[Var(Y|x,D)\\approx Var(f(x)|D)+\\sigma_\\epsilon^2.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["with torch.no_grad(): fmean,fvar=la(Xte,pred_type='glm')\n","fmean=fmean.squeeze(-1); fvar=fvar.squeeze(-1).squeeze(-1); pvar=fvar+la.sigma_noise**2; psd=torch.sqrt(pvar.clamp_min(1e-10))\n","mean_pred=fmean.numpy()*ys+ym; sd_pred=psd.numpy()*ys; lo=mean_pred-1.645*sd_pred; hi=mean_pred+1.645*sd_pred\n","coverage=np.mean((yte>=lo)&(yte<=hi)); print('90% predictive interval coverage:',round(float(coverage),3)); print('Average interval width:',round(float(np.mean(hi-lo)),3))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Future capacity distribution\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["future=np.array([[.90,31,.66,.72]],dtype=np.float32); xf=torch.tensor((future-Xm)/Xs)\n","with torch.no_grad(): fm,fv=la(xf,pred_type='glm')\n","mu=float(fm.squeeze())*ys+ym; sd=float(torch.sqrt(fv.squeeze()+la.sigma_noise**2))*ys\n","rng=np.random.default_rng(SEED); samples=np.clip(rng.normal(mu,sd,4000),0,None)\n","print('Predictive mean capacity:',round(mu,2)); print('5%,50%,95%:',np.quantile(samples,[.05,.5,.95]).round(2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Stochastic capacity reservation\n","\n","Suppose reserved capacity \(x\) costs money, but realized usable capacity cannot exceed the uncertain process capacity. A shortage penalty applies if delivered capacity falls below demand.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["S=500; scen=rng.choice(samples,S,replace=False); demand=110.; reserve_cost=1.6; shortage_penalty=10.\n","m=pyo.ConcreteModel(); m.S=pyo.RangeSet(0,S-1); m.x=pyo.Var(domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals,bounds=(0,150)); m.delivered=pyo.Var(m.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); m.shortage=pyo.Var(m.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals)\n","m.plan=pyo.Constraint(m.S,rule=lambda M,s:M.delivered[s]<=M.x); m.cap=pyo.Constraint(m.S,rule=lambda M,s:M.delivered[s]<=float(scen[s])); m.short=pyo.Constraint(m.S,rule=lambda M,s:M.shortage[s]>=demand-M.delivered[s])\n","m.obj=pyo.Objective(expr=reserve_cost*m.x+shortage_penalty*(1/S)*sum(m.shortage[s] for s in m.S))\n","res=pyo.SolverFactory('appsi_highs').solve(m); x_lap=pyo.value(m.x); print('Stochastic reservation:',round(x_lap,2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Mean-only baseline\n","\n","A deterministic policy ignores predictive spread and plans only from the posterior mean.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["x_mean=min(150.,mu); eval_s=rng.choice(samples,10000,replace=True)\n","def operational_loss(x,C):\n","    delivered=np.minimum(x,C); shortage=np.maximum(demand-delivered,0); return reserve_cost*x+shortage_penalty*shortage\n","rows=[]\n","for name,x in [('Mean-only',x_mean),('Laplace + stochastic optimization',x_lap)]:\n","    L=operational_loss(x,eval_s); q=np.quantile(L,.95); rows.append({'method':name,'reserved_capacity':x,'expected_cost':L.mean(),'CVaR95':L[L>=q].mean(),'shortage_probability':np.mean(np.minimum(x,eval_s)<demand)})\n","pd.DataFrame(rows).round(3)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Takeaway\n","\n","Laplace approximation is useful when a deterministic PyTorch model already exists and a post-hoc uncertainty layer is operationally attractive. It should still be compared with deep ensembles, Bayesian last layer, GP, and full BNN alternatives where feasible.\n"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}